<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0; font-size: 2em;">Lesson Planner – Theme # The Use of Technology in School – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Grade:</b> 9th Grade (CEFR: A2.4)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Scenario:</b> Technology in Education</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Theme:</b> The Use of Technology in School</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Draft a persuasive paragraph on a familiar topic. Interactive: Write daily observations about everyday situations and activities.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can draft a persuasive paragraph outlining the pros and cons of tech-free time during school hours (e.g., "While technology helps us stay informed, taking breaks can reduce eye strain and increase social interaction."). Can write daily observations about using technology at school (e.g., "Today, I used my tablet to look up information for my science project. It helped me find everything quickly and stay organized."). Can record observations on the benefits of technology for learning (e.g., "Using technology helps me learn faster because I can easily access resources and get immediate feedback on my work.").</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center; margin-top: 30px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276; width: 34%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays images of students using different technological devices (tablets, laptops, interactive whiteboards) in school. Students are asked to quickly jot down 2-3 words or short phrases about how they use "technology" in "school" (e.g., "research," "games," "presentations," "apps").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Modeling:</b> The teacher models sentences expressing opinions and suggestions using the simple present and modals "should"/"can." For example: "I think technology is *useful* for learning *because* we *can access* many *resources*." "We *should* sometimes *ignore* our *devices* during lunch for better social *interaction*." The teacher also explicitly models the stress in words like "education" and "innovative."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If something is 'beneficial,' is it a good thing or a bad thing?" (Expected answer: A good thing.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say, 'You *should* limit screen time,' am I telling you to do it or asking a question?" (Expected answer: Telling us/giving advice.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> 0-5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> The teacher provides students with two short model texts: 1) A short persuasive paragraph arguing for or against "tech-free time" in school, incorporating simple present opinions, modals, and discourse markers. 2) Two examples of "daily observations" from a student's diary about using "technology" in "school".</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>Example Persuasive Paragraph Snippet:</i> "While *technology* is very *beneficial* for finding information, I think we *should* have *tech-free* time during lunch. This *can* *solve* the *problem* of students ignoring each other. Instead, they *can engage* in real conversations."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>Example Daily Observation:</i> "Today, I *used* my *tablet* to *browse* for my science *project*. It *is* a *useful device* *because* I *can* easily *access* *resources* and keep my *progress* organized."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Communicative Competence:</b> Written Expression – Understanding and analyzing short written texts to extract specific information and recognize text structure.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students read the model texts.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> "What is the main idea of the persuasive paragraph?" (Expected: pros/cons of tech-free time). "What does the student observe about technology use?" (Expected: benefits for schoolwork).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Students match phrases from the texts to categories: "Benefit of Technology," "Drawback of Technology," "Suggestion for Use."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> 5-15 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Communicative Skill & Content:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar:</b> Simple present for expressing opinions and comparing preferences; Modal "should" for making suggestions; Modal "can" for expressing ability.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary:</b> technology, apps, tools, school, education, benefit, problem, solution, device, innovation, access, platform, software, resources, use, ignore, prefer, benefit, advise, solve, engage, incorporate, limit, recommend, browse, appropriate, useful, beneficial, innovative, educational, accessible, digital, technological, while, but, instead, because.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pragmatic:</b> Weighing benefits and drawbacks; Suggesting limits; Expressing opinions and comparing preferences.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Gap-Fill Opinions & Suggestions:</b> Students complete sentences with appropriate vocabulary (nouns, adjectives, verbs) and grammar (simple present, "should," "can") from a word bank, focusing on opinions and suggestions about technology.
                        <br><i>Example:</i> "I think *apps* ____ (be) *useful* for group *projects*." "We *should* ____ (limit) the use of *devices* during class."
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Sentence Transformation (Pros & Cons):</b> Students rewrite pairs of simple sentences into complex sentences using discourse markers (while, but, because) to express benefits and drawbacks or opinions.
                        <br><i>Example:</i> "Technology helps with research. Technology can be distracting." -> "While *technology* helps with *research*, it *can* be *distracting*." "I *prefer* digital *resources*. They are *accessible*." -> "I *prefer* digital *resources* *because* they *are accessible*."
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Peer Sentence Review:</b> In pairs, students write 3-4 sentences each, expressing an opinion about technology in school, a suggestion for its use, or a daily observation. They then exchange their sentences with their partner, checking for correct use of simple present, "should"/"can," and the target vocabulary. They can ask "What apps do you like the most?" during this exchange.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> 15-30 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task format:</b> Guided persuasive paragraph writing or daily observation entries.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task:</b> Students choose one of the following writing tasks, applying the language practiced:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Option A (Persuasive Paragraph):</b> Write a paragraph (5-7 sentences) arguing for or against "tech-free time" during a specific part of the school day (e.g., lunch, recess). The paragraph *should* outline at least one "pro" and one "con," use simple present for opinions, modals ("should," "can") for suggestions, and appropriate discourse markers (while, but, instead, because) to weigh benefits and drawbacks. Students *can* *recommend* a "solution" to a "problem."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Option B (Daily Observations):</b> Write 2-3 short "daily observations" about how they (or other students) *use technology* at "school" today or this week. Each observation *should* include a specific example of *technology* use (e.g., "apps," "device," "software") and an opinion on its *benefit* or a *problem* it *solves*. For example, "Today, I *used* my *computer* to *create* a presentation. It *is* a *beneficial tool* *because* I *can* easily *incorporate* images."</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Action:</b> Circulate, offer support, clarify vocabulary, and provide gentle correction on grammar or sentence structure, focusing on the clarity of their written message.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> 30-40 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Assessment Task:</b> Students submit their chosen written piece (persuasive paragraph or daily observations).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Observation/Rubric):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity & Cohesion:</b> Is the main idea clear? Is the paragraph/observation well-structured?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar Accuracy:</b> Correct use of simple present for opinions, modals "should" and "can" for suggestions/ability.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary Use:</b> Incorporation of at least 5-7 target vocabulary words (e.g., technology, benefit, problem, solution, useful, accessible, integrate, limit, recommend).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pragmatic Competence:</b> Effectively weighing benefits/drawbacks and/or suggesting limits/expressing opinions.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following questions on a small slip of paper:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What new words or phrases did you use in your writing today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was the most challenging part of writing your paragraph/observations?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> 40-45 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How well did I express my ideas about technology in school in writing today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one thing I would do differently next time I write about this topic?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this writing lesson? (e.g., clear models, structured practice, peer feedback)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson to further support students' writing ability and integration of language content? (e.g., more practice with specific discourse markers, clearer sentence starters for complex ideas).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Connection to next lesson:</b> This writing practice on expressing opinions and providing suggestions will be crucial for Lesson 5, where students will need to consolidate information and present their project ideas (e.g., suggesting an innovative *solution* using *technology* in *education*) in a coherent manner, which often involves some form of written planning or summarization.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> 45-50 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>